/cmake-build-debug/*
/build*/
/var/*
!/var/build/.gitkeep
!/var/ccache/.gitkeep
/env/dist/*
!/env/dist/.gitkeep
/env/user/*
/.env*
.idea
!.gitkeep

# do not ignore the ccache folder (used by the ci)
!/var/docker/ccache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Directories the image never uses. Added 2026-08-24 because the build
# context had grown to 2.2GB and every ship paid for it in transfer time --
# several minutes per build, on a night with eight of them.
#
# apps/docker/Dockerfile (all four targets: build, authserver, worldserver,
# db-import, client-data) copies exactly this and nothing else:
#
#     CMakeLists.txt   conf/   deps/   src/   modules/   apps/   data/
#
# Everything below is host-side working material. If a COPY is ever added
# for one of these, delete its line here deliberately rather than wondering
# why the file is missing inside the image.
#
#   tools/       1.9GB -- launcher/target (Rust artifacts, rebuilt by every
#                build_launcher.py run), ws-layer.tar and ws-extract/ (an
#                unpacked worldserver image), client-patch dist/cache/staging
#   azerothcore/ 523MB -- a stray copy of a built env/dist
#   archive/     123MB -- retired experiments, kept for reference only
/tools/
/azerothcore/
/archive/
/doc/
/bin/

# DO NOT exclude /.git/ -- tried on 2026-08-24 and the build fails immediately:
#
#   ERROR: failed to calculate checksum of ref ...: "/.git": not found
#
# apps/docker/Dockerfile line 96 bind-mounts it at build time
# (--mount=type=bind,target=/azerothcore/.git,source=.git) so genrev can stamp
# the revision without the repo ending up inside the image. A bind mount still
# needs the path present in the build CONTEXT, so ignoring it breaks the build
# rather than merely losing the version banner.
#
# It is 2.27GB and it is the bulk of what remains. If build time becomes painful
# again, the lever is a shallower repo or a build arg that skips genrev -- not
# this file.
#
# Worth knowing when auditing what the context needs: grep the Dockerfile for
# `source=` as well as COPY and ADD. Only checking COPY is what caused the
# failed attempt above.
